      "file_path": "/home/skogix/skogai/CLAUDE.md",
      "old_string": "## Current Development Focus\n\nBased on git status, active work includes:\n- Lore system enhancements (new lore files being added)\n- Agent system development (new agents directory)\n- Logging infrastructure (logs directory additions)\n\nThe project follows a \"develop\" branch workflow with \"master\" as the main branch for PRs.",
      "new_string": "## Discovered Workflows and Patterns\n\n### Anti-Pattern: Creating Theoretical Infrastructure\nNEVER spend time creating elaborate scaffolding without testing if basic functionality works.\nThis causes: Frustration and wasted effort on non-functional systems.\nInstead: Always verify existing tools work first, then enhance incrementally.\nEvidence: Attempted to create complex documentation agent system before checking that `documentor` agent already existed and was functional.\n\n### Workflow Improvement: Agent Discovery Before Creation\nWhen needing agent functionality, always:\n1. Check if agent exists: `argc list@agent`\n2. Test existing agent: `argc run@agent <name> <action> <json>`\n3. Only create new agents if functionality truly missing\nEvidence: Found working `documentor` agent already integrated with argc ecosystem after initially trying to build from scratch.\n\n### Documentation Agent Usage Pattern\nUse the `documentor` agent for automated documentation:\n```bash\n# Generate code documentation\nargc run@agent documentor generate_code_docs '{\"path\": \"/path/to/file\"}'\n\n# Create lore entries (chronicles evolution)\nargc run@agent documentor generate_lore '{\"topic\": \"Feature Name\"}'\n\n# Index memory system\nargc run@agent documentor index_memory '{\"project\": \"skogai\"}'\n\n# Review documentation quality\nargc run@agent documentor review_docs '{\"path\": \"/docs/\"}'\n```\nContext: Agent outputs to `./docs/code/` and integrates with basic-memory for lore storage.\nSuccess indicator: Files generated in appropriate directories, basic-memory integration confirmed.\n\n### Tool Usage: Built-in Claude Code Agents\nPrefer using Claude Code's Task tool with existing subagents:\n- `technical-writer`: For documentation after feature completion\n- `architect`: For system-level documentation and analysis\n- `researcher`: For understanding existing systems without modification\nThese understand SkogAI notation and multi-agent architecture natively.\nEvidence: Successfully used Task tool to generate comprehensive project documentation.\n\n## Current Development Focus\n\nBased on git status, active work includes:\n- Lore system enhancements (new lore files being added)\n- Agent system development (new agents directory)\n- Logging infrastructure (logs directory additions)\n- Documentation automation using `documentor` agent\n\nThe project follows a \"develop\" branch workflow with \"master\" as the main branch for PRs."
    }
